Don't turn warnings into errors in the Linux clang build.

The Linux CMake builds PhysX with -Werror -Weverything. -Weverything enables
every warning the compiler knows, so each new clang release adds warnings the
pinned PhysX source doesn't silence, and the build fails on a toolchain newer
than the one NVIDIA tested with (clang 22: -Wmissing-include-dirs, -Wnrvo,
-Wformat-signedness). Keep the warnings, drop -Werror, so the SDK builds with
any current clang.

diff --git a/physx/source/compiler/cmake/linux/CMakeLists.txt b/physx/source/compiler/cmake/linux/CMakeLists.txt
index 312cf89..4f389b3 100644
--- a/physx/source/compiler/cmake/linux/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/physx/source/compiler/cmake/linux/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 STRING(TOLOWER "${CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE}" CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE_LOWERCASE)
 
 #TODO: Fix warnings
-SET(CLANG_WARNINGS "-ferror-limit=0 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Weverything\
+SET(CLANG_WARNINGS "-ferror-limit=0 -Wall -Wextra -Weverything\
     -Wno-unused-but-set-variable \
     -Wno-switch-default \
     -Wno-cast-qual \
